 "final_text": "Submitted. Summary for the board-call reply to Robin:\n\n**CESP four-week cash forecast (starting Mon 3/2, per TRS-SOP-004 direct-method weekly assumptions):**\n\n- **Week 1 (3/2\u20133/8): +$14,000** \u2014 Program-fee receipt ($42K) outpaces a stage-buildout payable ($28K).\n- **Week 2 (3/9\u20133/15): \u2212$169,000** \u2014 Biweekly payroll funding ($185K) swamps modest AR/AP flows.\n- **Week 3 (3/16\u20133/22): +$51,000** \u2014 A program-fee prepay collects with no offsetting outflows.\n- **Week 4 (3/23\u20133/29): \u2212$218,000** \u2014 Second payroll funding ($185K) plus an AV-equipment payable ($33K), with no receipts due.\n- **Four-week net: \u2212$322,000**\n\nThe two payroll fundings are the swing factor \u2014 CESP has no AR due in either payroll week large enough to offset them. Only 3 open AR and 3 open AP items exist for CESP in the ERP, all captured above; no other receipts/disbursements fall in the window, and no other payroll dates are in the payroll calendar file for this period. Per SOP, this is flows only \u2014 no opening cash balance was rolled in.",
